{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <cstring>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint n, k, p;\n\nlong long mod_pow(long long base, int exp) {\n    long long result = 1;\n    base %= p;\n    while (exp > 0) {\n        if (exp & 1) result = (result * base) % p;\n        base = (base * base) % p;\n        exp >>= 1;\n    }\n    return result;\n}\n\nint get_lowbit(int x) {\n    return x & -x;\n}\n\nlong long dp[26][250010];\nlong long factorial[250010];\nlong long inv_factorial[250010];\n\nvoid precompute() {\n    factorial[0] = 1;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n        factorial[i] = (factorial[i-1] * i) % p;\n    }\n    inv_factorial[n] = mod_pow(factorial[n], p-2);\n    for (int i = n; i > 0; --i) {\n        inv_factorial[i-1] = (inv_factorial[i] * i) % p;\n    }\n}\n\nlong long compute(int level, int mask) {\n    if (dp[level][mask] != -1) return dp[level][mask];\n    \n    if (mask == 0) {\n        dp[level][mask] = factorial[n];\n        for (int i = 1; i <= level; ++i) {\n            dp[level][mask] = (dp[level][mask] * (k - i + 1)) % p;\n        }\n        return dp[level][mask];\n    }\n    \n    dp[level][mask] = 0;\n    int complement = mask - get_lowbit(mask);\n    for (int subset = complement; subset; subset = (subset - 1) & complement) {\n        dp[level][mask] = (dp[level][mask] + inv_factorial[mask - subset] * compute(level + 1, subset)) % p;\n    }\n    dp[level][mask] = (dp[level][mask] + inv_factorial[mask] * compute(level + 1, 0)) % p;\n    return dp[level][mask];\n}\n\nint main() {\n    scanf(\"%d %d %d\", &n, &k, &p);\n    \n    long long total = 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        total = (total * k) % p;\n    }\n    \n    if (n % 2 == 0) {\n        precompute();\n        memset(dp, -1, sizeof(dp));\n        total = (total - compute(0, n) + p) % p;\n    }\n    \n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", total);\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static int n, k, p;\n    static long[][] dp;\n    static long[] factorial;\n    static long[] inv_factorial;\n\n    static long mod_pow(long base, int exp) {\n        long result = 1;\n        base %= p;\n        while (exp > 0) {\n            if ((exp & 1) == 1) result = (result * base) % p;\n            base = (base * base) % p;\n            exp >>= 1;\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n\n    static int get_lowbit(int x) {\n        return x & -x;\n    }\n\n    static void precompute() {\n        factorial[0] = 1;\n        for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n            factorial[i] = (factorial[i-1] * i) % p;\n        }\n        inv_factorial[n] = mod_pow(factorial[n], p-2);\n        for (int i = n; i > 0; --i) {\n            inv_factorial[i-1] = (inv_factorial[i] * i) % p;\n        }\n    }\n\n    static long compute(int level, int mask) {\n        if (dp[level][mask] != -1) return dp[level][mask];\n        \n        if (mask == 0) {\n            dp[level][mask] = factorial[n];\n            for (int i = 1; i <= level; ++i) {\n                dp[level][mask] = (dp[level][mask] * (k - i + 1)) % p;\n            }\n            return dp[level][mask];\n        }\n        \n        dp[level][mask] = 0;\n        int complement = mask - get_lowbit(mask);\n        for (int subset = complement; subset != 0; subset = (subset - 1) & complement) {\n            dp[level][mask] = (dp[level][mask] + inv_factorial[mask - subset] * compute(level + 1, subset)) % p;\n        }\n        dp[level][mask] = (dp[level][mask] + inv_factorial[mask] * compute(level + 1, 0)) % p;\n        return dp[level][mask];\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        n = sc.nextInt();\n        k = sc.nextInt();\n        p = sc.nextInt();\n        \n        long total = 1;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n            total = (total * k) % p;\n        }\n        \n        if (n % 2 == 0) {\n            factorial = new long[250010];\n            inv_factorial = new long[250010];\n            dp = new long[26][250010];\n            for (int i = 0; i < 26; ++i) {\n                Arrays.fill(dp[i], -1);\n            }\n            precompute();\n            total = (total - compute(0, n) + p) % p;\n        }\n        \n        System.out.println(total);\n        sc.close();\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00018821375851985067, -2.264974000354414e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -0.000342191313393414, -2.5152843591058627e-05, -0.023340249434113503, -0.5298593044281006, -1.9073304429184645e-05, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -3.3378044463461265e-05, -0.01416497677564621, -0.00015889335190877318, -0.00769933732226491, -0.0003943857445847243, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -2.622600959512056e-06, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -2.2172682292875834e-05, -1.311301275563892e-06, -0.005234109237790108, -0.0021873614750802517, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -0.00017128908075392246, -0.05585623160004616, -3.218